8) VM loop (pseudocode)
The VM is compact, JIT-friendly, and exposes intrinsics to the runtime.

vm_run(bytecode):
    ip = entry
    while true:
        opcode = fetch_byte(ip)
        switch opcode:
            case OP_LOAD_CONST:
                reg = fetch_reg(ip)
                idx = fetch_u16(ip)
                regs[reg] = constant_pool[idx]
            case OP_CALL_INTRIN:
                intrin_idx = fetch_u16(ip)
                argc = fetch_u8(ip)
                args = pop_args(argc)
                result = runtime.intrin_dispatch(intrin_idx, args)
                push(result)
            case OP_BUILD_TX:
                template_idx = fetch_u16(ip)
                reg = build_template(constant_pool[template_idx])
                push(reg)
            case OP_PATCH_SIGN:
                template_reg = fetch_reg(ip)
                nonce_reg = fetch_reg(ip)
                gas_reg = fetch_reg(ip)
                keyref = fetch_u16(ip)
                runtime.patch_and_sign(template_reg, nonce_reg, gas_reg, keyref)
            case OP_MEMPOOL_SUBSCRIBE:
                filter_idx = fetch_u16(ip)
                runtime.mempool_subscribe(constant_pool[filter_idx], vm_context)
            case OP_VECTOR_OP:
                opid = fetch_u8(ip)
                dest = fetch_reg(ip)
                a = fetch_reg(ip); b = fetch_reg(ip)
                regs[dest] = vector_execute(opid, regs[a], regs[b])
            case OP_JMP:
                offset = fetch_i32(ip); ip += offset
            case OP_JMP_IF_FALSE:
                cond = pop()
                if not cond: ip += fetch_i32(ip)
            case OP_YIELD:
                runtime.scheduler.yield_current(vm_context)
            case OP_HALT:
                return
        end switch
Key runtime responsibilities:

intrin_dispatch implements the 20 built-ins and lowers expensive ops to optimized native functions (C/Rust) — e.g., find_arb runs the route engine and can call GPU kernels or SIMD functions.

Scheduler can pause VM when waiting for async I/O (rpc results, mempool events). Hot code annotated @no_heap yields rarely.

